{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anti-inflammatory, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "NMR", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is most similar (45.5%) to bacterial P15s. Discovered from the human unconventional myosin 1h protein by computer prediction. Activity: Active against E. coli ATCC 25922 and 4 strains (MIC 1-2 uM), P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 and 8 strains (MIC 1.67-8.2 uM), S. aureus ATCC 25923 and 3 strains (MIC 1-4.1 uM), E. faecalis ATCC 29212 (MIC 2-8.2 uM). In a different paper,it is showed to be active against S. epidermidis (MIC 1 uM), T. rubrum (MIC 8 uM), and C. albicans (MIC 1.67 uM). In vitro Toxicity: human RBC: not hemo.lytic (HC50 >128 uM). Structure: In DPC micelles, residues 3-14 of Hs02 adopted a helical structure. You can rotate, zoom, and view the 3D structure here in the PDB. Anti-inflammatory: HS02 suppressed the LPS-primed release of TNF-alpha, thereby anti-inflammatory. Updated 8/2019; 7/2021; 11/2023", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31340580", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Int J Mol Sci. 2019 Jul 23;20(14). pii: E3604. doi: 10.3390/ijms20143604. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03104", "source_id": "AP03104", "source_numeric_id": "03104", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03104", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Intragenic Antimicrobial Peptide Hs02 Hampers the Proliferation of Single- and Dual-Species Biofilms of P. aeruginosa and S. aureus: A Promising Agent for Mitigation of Biofilm-Associated Infections", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
